The inclusion criteria were:

diagnosed as sepsis according to the Third International Consensus Definitions for Sepsis and Septic Shock (Sepsis-3) [ 14 ] ;

aged above 18 years old.

The exclusion criteria were:

complicated with other fatal diseases (e.g., hematologic malignancies and solid tumors);

infected with human immunodeficiency virus (HIV);

transferred from other hospitals;

received immunosuppressive therapy within 3 months before enrollment;

pregnant or lactating women.
